fact WorkItem(id: "WI-994", description: some(value: "Variant-exposure link is order-dependent: `namespace X` before `sort X { entity V }` leaves bare `V` unresolvable from the enclosing scope.\n\nFOUND WHILE DRIVING WI-979, and the obvious fix was TRIED AND REVERTED there --\nthe revert is the finding, so read it before re-attempting.\n\nTHE DEFECT. scan_items_pass1's Item::SortWithBody arm gates the variant-exposure\nlink on `is_new && has_variant` (kb/load.rs ~2771). Measured, on a NON-eponymous\nsort (the eponymous shape cannot see this -- with `entity Rec` inside `sort Rec`\nthe bare name resolves as the sort itself, so the link is never consulted):\n\n  namespace vb\n    namespace Colour  operation twice(c: Colour) -> Int64 = 2  end\n    sort Colour  entity Red(v: Int64)  end\n    operation drive() -> Int64 = Red(v: 5).twice()\n  end\n    => 10:32: type mismatch in Red.apply: expected known operation or\n              arrow-typed variable, got unknown functor\n  CONTROL, the same two declarations swapped  => loads clean, drive() = 2\n\nSame class as WI-979's category loss -- a fact read off WHICH DECLARATION CAME\nFIRST rather than off the declarations -- and reachable through exactly the pair\nproposal 059 R2 blesses. Pinned in both directions by\nwi979_declaration_order_test::variant_exposure_is_still_order_dependent_wi984,\nwhich uses expect_load_errors, so when this lands that test FAILS and the fix\ncannot arrive silently.\n\nWHY `if has_variant` ALONE IS WRONG -- MEASURED, this is the whole ticket.\n`is_new` is false for TWO unrelated populations, and un-gating serves the wrong\none:\n  (a) declaration-reuse -- `namespace X` (or `entity X`) already defined the\n      name. This is the case that wants the link.\n  (b) BOOTSTRAP-reuse -- register_prelude pre-registered the symbol. Measured:\n      anthill.prelude.{List, Option, TypeExtractor, EffectExpression} and\n      anthill.reflect.{MemberKind, Expr, Pattern} are all pre-registered and then\n      re-declared with variants in stdlib source. Un-gating hands all seven an\n      exposure link they never had -- ~55 short names newly bare-resolvable from\n      anthill.prelude / anthill.reflect.\n\nDRIVEN CONSEQUENCE of (b), the reason for the revert:\n\n  namespace p\n    import anthill.prelude.*\n    import anthill.reflect.*\n    operation p(t: Type, g: List[T = Term]) -> EffectExpression\n      = guarded(label: t, guard: g)\n  end\n\n  with `has_variant` alone => ambiguous symbol 'guarded': candidates\n      [\"anthill.prelude.EffectExpression.guarded\",\n       \"anthill.reflect.LogicalQuery.guarded\"]\n  gated (today)              => resolves uniquely to LogicalQuery.guarded\n\nTHE FULL WORKSPACE SUITE STAYED GREEN THROUGH THIS. There is exactly one wildcard\nimport in the repo (inside a parse test), so nothing in-tree trips it. A green\nsuite was not evidence, and will not be for the real fix either -- this ticket\nneeds its own ambiguity guard.\n\nSECOND CONSEQUENCE, also driven: un-gating half-wires the shape 059 R1 refuses.\n`entity Rec(n)` + `sort Rec { entity Inner }` starts loading clean with bare\n`Inner` resolving OUT of the sort, while the body still cannot see IN, because\nthe ENCLOSING link (load.rs ~2725) stays `is_new`-gated. Variants leak out of a\nscope whose body resolves nothing. WI-979's pinning test for that shape was blind\nto it (its fixture had no variant); the fixture now carries one.\n\nWHAT THE FIX NEEDS: a predicate that tells declaration-reuse from bootstrap-reuse.\n`is_new` cannot -- it is false for both. Candidates worth measuring: whether the\nexisting symbol was defined by `define` (scope-local) vs `define_qualified_only`\n(which is what register_prelude uses, and which deliberately does NOT insert into\nany scope's locals); or recording the reuse REASON at the site.\n\nALSO CONSIDER, same arm, same class: the ENCLOSING link at load.rs ~2725 is\n`is_new`-gated too. Left refused deliberately under WI-979 because 059 R1 refuses\n`entity X` + `sort X` outright -- do not un-gate it without that verdict.\n\nACCEPTANCE: both declaration orders resolve a bare variant from the enclosing\nscope; the sort-first control still passes; a GUARD test asserts the wildcard-import\n`guarded` case still resolves uniquely (it is the regression the naive fix causes,\nand no existing test covers it); the `entity X` + `sort X` shape still fails\nloudly; variant_exposure_is_still_order_dependent_wi984 is flipped to assert\nsuccess rather than pinned failure. cargo-test green via rustland/scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-08-04T21:36:54Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-994", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED as a PLAIN UN-GATE (`if has_variant`), NOT the declaration-vs-bootstrap\npredicate this ticket prescribed. User decision, 2026-08-04, after the measurement\nbelow. Two of this ticket's own claims were wrong.\n\nTHE CONTROL THIS TICKET LACKED, and it inverts population (b). Under `import\nanthill.prelude.*`:\n    bare `pair`      (enum anthill.prelude.Pair, NOT pre-registered)  => RESOLVES\n    bare `merge`     (enum anthill.prelude.EffectExpression, pre-reg) => unknown functor\n    bare `empty_row` (same enum)                                      => unknown functor\nSame namespace, same wildcard, same `enum ... entity ...` shape. So the 7 bootstrap\nsorts are not a population that \"never had the link\" — they are 7 sorts whose §8.6\nexposure the bootstrap silently DELETES. A pre-registration is the loader's own\nstand-in for the SAME declaration, so gating on it made the exposure read off which\nREGISTRATION came first — the very class of bug this ticket is about, one level down.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERION 3 WAS INVERTED for the same reason. It asked for a guard that\nthe double-wildcard `guarded` \"still resolves uniquely\". Measured, that unique\nresolution was the loader binding a name the author never chose: the fixture spells\n`guarded(label:, guard:)` — unmistakably EffectExpression.guarded — and the loader\nbound LogicalQuery.guarded, then reported `'guarded' has no field 'label' (declares:\nquery, condition)`. §8.6: two sorts exposing one variant name make the bare name\nAMBIGUOUS \"rather than letting one silently win\" — the verdict anthill-cli's\nambiguous-symbol.anthill already pins for two wildcard-imported SORTS. The guard test\nnow asserts the ambiguity; a single-wildcard CONTROL pins that `guarded` still\nresolves uniquely and passes either way.\n\nThe `define` vs `define_qualified_only` candidate this ticket suggested is also\nrefuted: register_stdlib_scopes uses `define` (scope-local) for all 7, so that\npredicate cannot tell the populations apart either.\n\nSECOND CONSEQUENCE DISSOLVED, not handled. `entity X` + `sort X` is refused outright\nby 059 R1 / WI-997, so the \"half-wired\" shape is a load error and no program reaches\na KB built from it. The ENCLOSING link stays `is_new`-gated — and the reason is\nstronger than symmetry: for both reuse populations that link is ALREADY on the scope\nwhen this arm runs (Item::Namespace adds it on the same hash-consed nullary term;\nregister_stdlib_scopes adds one per pre-registered sort), so un-gating it would\nre-offer a present link rather than supply a missing one. The one shape it genuinely\ngates out is `entity X` + `sort X`, where a free-standing entity built no scope.\n\nA REGRESSION THE UN-GATE INTRODUCED, found by review and FIXED here. `is_new` had\nbeen capping the exposure link at one push per name as a side effect. load_incremental\nre-scans files already in the KB — three idempotence tests do exactly that — so\nwithout the cap every reload pushed another copy: anthill.prelude 28 -> 56 exposure\nparents on the second load, unbounded in the number of loads, and silent (the WI-997\nledger is per scan_definitions call, so it reports no duplicate declaration).\nSymbolTable::add_parent is now IDEMPOTENT per distinct ScopeInclusion — the set\nsemantics resolution already assumes (visited-guarded walk, matches deduped by\nsymbol). Dedup is on the WHOLE inclusion, so two links differing only in\ninstantiation_term_raw (one spec required at two instantiations) both stand.\n\nTESTS. wi994_variant_exposure_test (4, new) + intern::tests::\nadd_parent_is_idempotent_per_distinct_inclusion (new) + wi979_declaration_order_test::\nvariant_exposure_is_order_independent_wi994 (flipped from expect_load_errors).\nBacking each change out was RUN, not predicted: restoring `is_new &&` fails 3 of the\nnew/flipped tests and leaves both controls green; deleting add_parent's guard makes\nthe idempotence assertion read 3.\n\nFULL WORKSPACE: 4110 passed, 0 failed (baseline 4105 + 5 new).\n\nFOUND, PINNED, NOT FIXED -> WI-1005. The ambiguity is reported TWICE for one\noccurrence, once per scope it is remapped in (the operation's, the enclosing\nnamespace's). dedup_key is deliberately injective and the two renderings differ only\nin the scope name. Easy to miss: name the namespace and the operation alike and they\ncoincide and dedup — which is what hid it from the probe this ticket's test was\nwritten from (4 errors) until the fixture renamed the namespace (5).\n\nNOT DONE, recorded rather than fired: the \"drive an op, assert the built entity's\nfunctor QN\" shape is hand-rolled at 9 sites across 5 test files (eval_test,\nwi818_executable_backing_test, wi204_sort_param_test, wi858_pair_orderings_test) and\nthis ticket adds 2 more; tests/common/mod.rs documents lifting such a shape at the\nSECOND live copy. A local helper covers this file; the lift is a migration of its own.", at: "2026-08-04T21:36:51Z")
